# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS, the first-commitment fork (v25 prep draft, 10-23).
# Syntax: header of build.py, plus the v25 keys shape:, kind:, rungs:, fork: (moments) and aim: (options),
# aims-shape.md section 4. Pours into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib (POUR-NOTES.md).
# Twenty moments, two per ladder shape: kind plateau, fork go_on, rung 0 only. A life that has just taken up an aim
# meets its first real test (the first fee, the step up from the beginners, the first refusal, the first winter, the
# novelty wearing off) and decides whether to go on. Every moment offers going on, a change of approach, easing off or
# putting it off (aim: ease) and letting it go (aim: stop); a stop always leaves a lesson, a skill mark or a person.
# Layout: the five one-colour ways, then one full cross cycle, alternating by moment:
#   s1 W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W (the first moment of each shape)   s2 W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U (the second)
# Ages: competition, craft, art and knowledge open to children (no money gains, no nights out under 12); career from
# 16; home from 18; cause from 13; land, faith and venture from 14 to 16.

# ================================================================ COMPETITION

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- competition: first step, fork go_on (cycle s1)

== the first term's fee falls due
tier: life event
shape: competition
kind: plateau
rungs: 0
fork: go_on
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: leisure, money, friends
horizon: months
roles: parent, friend, mentor
earth: the free beginners' weeks of {aim.doing} are over, and the first term's fee falls due before the next session
tribal: the first moons of {aim.doing} are over, and the elders ask which of the young ones will keep at it through the cold
magic: the guild's trial weeks at {aim.doing} are over, and the first term's fee falls due at the month's end
scene: The free beginners' weeks at {aim.place} are over. The sign-on sheet for the full term goes round today, and the fee is due before the next session. {N} has liked {aim.doing} so far, mostly, but liking it and signing on are not quite the same thing.
scene tribal: The first moons of {aim.doing} are over, and the young ones who tried it are being counted. At the new moon the elders will ask who means to keep at it through the cold, and who goes back to other work.
scene magic: The guild's trial weeks at {aim.doing} are over, and the clerk has posted the first term's fee by the door. It falls due at the month's end, and only the names of those who pay go on the rolls.
- W | sign on for the full term, and turn up to every session it covers | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 85
- U | ask what the term actually teaches, and sign on only for the part that helps | v: self-direction, security | aim: work | foot: lesson ask what it covers | chance: 75
- B | sign on, and ask to be moved up to the stronger group straight away | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | skip the fee, and play for fun wherever a game turns up | v: hedonism, stimulation | aim: ease | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 85
- G | stop here, glad of the start, and keep the friends from the beginners' weeks | v: benevolence, security | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 90
- W>U | sign on, and keep a notebook of every session to see what changes | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- U>B | wait a term, and watch how the regulars do it before paying to join | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: later | foot: lesson watching teaches too | chance: 85
- B>R | sign on, and ask to be entered in {aim.contest} before the term is out | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 60
- R>G | sign on together with a friend, so neither of them drops out alone | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G>W | let it go for now, and help out at {aim.place} on the open days instead | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: stop | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
works: The question is settled, and the next weeks feel lighter for it, whichever way it went.
works: {N} stops turning it over on the way home, and the choice starts to feel like {Ns} own.
fails: The choice sits uneasily for a while, and {N} half wishes it had gone the other way.
fails: A small row at home about the fee, or about the lack of one, takes a week to blow over.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- competition: first step, fork go_on (cycle s2)

== the beginners' group moves up
tier: life event
shape: competition
kind: plateau
rungs: 0
fork: go_on
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-80
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: leisure, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, mentor, rival
earth: the beginners' group at {aim.place} is folded into the main session from next week, faster and harder
tribal: the young ones who began {aim.doing} this season are to train beside the grown ones from the next moon
magic: the novices at {aim.doing} are to join the full drills of the tower's long hall from next week
scene: The beginners' group at {aim.place} is being folded into the main session from next week: faster, harder, alongside people who have been {aim.doing} for years. The first few weeks were easy to enjoy. This next part will not be, at least not at first.
scene tribal: From the next moon the young ones who began {aim.doing} this season will train beside the grown ones, who do not slow down for anyone. Several of the young have already gone quiet about it.
scene magic: From next week the novices join the full drills in the tower's long hall, where the seniors do not slow down for anyone. The masters will watch who keeps up, and who keeps coming.
- W | move up with the group as planned, and keep to every session | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | ask to stay with the newcomers a few more weeks, and move up when ready | v: self-direction, security | aim: later | foot: lesson ready beats early | chance: 85
- B | move up, and pick out the best one there to measure against | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R | try one session at the harder level, and decide on the spot | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson try it before deciding | chance: 75
- G | let it go before it stops being fun, and keep in touch with the group | v: benevolence, hedonism | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 90
- W>B | move up, and do the extra drills the main group expects of newcomers | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- U>R | find another place where beginners keep a session of their own | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: place gather.games | chance: 70
- B>G | move up, but only every other week, and practise at home in between | v: achievement, security | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- R>W | move up, and make a point of welcoming the next beginner through the door | v: stimulation, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 80
- G>U | stop, and take what the first weeks taught into something calmer | v: security, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: lesson a start is never wasted | chance: 88
works: The first harder weeks are rough, and then, without anyone saying so, they are just the weeks.
works: The choice holds, and {N} finds a pace that can be kept.
fails: The step up shows every weak spot at once, and {N} goes home sore and doubtful.
fails: Whatever was chosen, {N} keeps glancing back at the other way for a while.

# ================================================================ CRAFT

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- craft: first step, fork go_on (cycle s1)

== the first real piece comes out wrong
tier: life event
shape: craft
kind: plateau
rungs: 0
fork: go_on
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 9-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: interests, work
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, parent
earth: the first real piece of {aim.doing} has come out wrong, and the materials for the next must be ordered this week
tribal: the first thing {N} has made for the clan's use has cracked, and the elders wait to see if {N} will try again
magic: the first true piece {N} has made in the workrooms has come out crooked, and the master wants an answer
scene: After weeks of practice pieces, the first real one is finished, and it has come out wrong: crooked where it should be true, rough where it should be smooth. The materials for the next piece have to be ordered by the end of the week, if {N} wants a next piece at all.
scene tribal: The first thing {N} has made for the clan's use cracked on its first day, and the others saw it. The elders say nothing, and wait to see whether {N} will come back to the work.
scene magic: The first true piece {N} has made in the workrooms is crooked, and it sits on the bench for everyone to see. The master asks, before the week is out, whether {N} means to begin another.
- W | order the materials, and make the same piece again, step by step as taught | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- U | take the spoiled piece apart, and find exactly where it went wrong | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson the mistake shows the way | chance: 75
- B | ask the best hand at {aim.place} to look at it and say what is wrong | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- R | start something completely different, just to get the fun of it back | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: work | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 80
- G | leave the order for a month, and let the disappointment settle first | v: security, tradition | aim: later | foot: lesson disappointment settles with time | chance: 88
- W>U | make the next piece smaller and simpler, and get one thing right | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson small and right first | chance: 85
- U>B | let it go, and keep the eye for good work that it trained | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: stop | foot: lesson a trained eye stays | chance: 85
- B>R | keep the crooked piece in plain sight, and beat it on the next try | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson pride can be a spur | chance: 65
- R>G | stop for good, and give the crooked piece to someone who will like it anyway | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 90
- G>W | go on, but only in the class sessions, with no extra hours at home | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 88
works: Within the month the crooked piece stops stinging, and {N} can look at it and almost smile.
works: The choice settles, and {N} finds the hands still remember what they learned.
fails: The spoiled piece stays on {Ns} mind longer than it deserves.
fails: The next weeks are flat and unsure, whichever way it went.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- craft: first step, fork go_on (cycle s2)

== the weeks of nothing but the basics
tier: life event
shape: craft
kind: plateau
rungs: 0
fork: go_on
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 10-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: interests, learning
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, rival
earth: the course in {aim.doing} has slowed into weeks of nothing but the basics, and next term's sign-up is due
tribal: the old ones set the young to the same plain task, day after day, and ask who will stay for the rest
magic: the masters set the novices at {aim.doing} to the same plain exercise for a month, and ask who will stay
scene: The exciting part is over. For weeks now {aim.doing} at {aim.place} has been nothing but the basics: measuring, preparing, the same plain exercise again and again, nothing to take home. Sign-up for next term closes on Friday, and the novelty that carried {N} this far has worn thin.
scene tribal: For a moon the old ones have set the young to the same plain task, day after day, and nothing of it is used. Before the next moon they will ask who stays to learn the rest.
scene magic: For a month the masters have set the novices to the same plain exercise, and nobody has been allowed to make anything real. The rolls for the next term close at the week's end.
- W | sign up again, and do the plain work as carefully as the rest | v: conformity, tradition | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | ask what each plain exercise is for, and practise with that in mind | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson every drill has a reason | chance: 80
- B | turn the basics into a race, and be the quickest clean hand in the group | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R | make something small and real at home on the side, to keep the spark | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- G | let it go, and keep the few plain skills for mending things at home | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 90
- W>B | sign up, and ask the teacher for a harder version of each exercise | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- U>R | find a teacher who teaches the basics through real pieces | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: person teacher | chance: 65
- B>G | skip a term, and come back when the household's weeks are less full | v: achievement, security | aim: later | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- R>W | stop for good, and teach a younger one the bits already learned | v: stimulation, universalism | aim: stop | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
- G>U | keep at it slowly, one session a week, and stop worrying about the pace | v: security, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: lesson slow still gets there | chance: 88
works: The plain weeks end at last, and the next thing feels earned.
works: The choice holds, and {N} finds a pace for {aim.doing} that does not grind.
fails: The boredom lingers whichever way it went, and {N} waits for it to lift.
fails: The decision is made, but the doubt about it takes a few weeks to fade.

